**Full-page sweep** (`sweep4.js` then `sweep4b.js`): enumerated every
focusable element via a real-Tab-modality bounded walk (see methodology
note), on /dashboard, /whatif, /major-expenses, /insights (June range), at
1300, both themes, opening every `<details>` first. `sweep4b.js` additionally
walks each element's ancestor chain for the first non-transparent
`background-color` AND flags `background-image` != `none` anywhere in the
chain (so nav's real gradient — the source of attempt-1's false reading —
is caught and excluded rather than trusted). Of 87-1753 focusable elements
per page, computed-style-verified low-contrast (<3:1) hits with a
**non-gradient**, directly-reported background:

  light-/whatif   BUTTON #whatif-new-scenario-toggle  outline rgb(79,70,229) on bg rgb(79,70,229)  contrast=1.00
  light-/whatif   BUTTON #add-chain-step-btn            outline rgb(79,70,229) on bg rgb(79,70,229)  contrast=1.00
  light-/whatif   BUTTON .projection-display-toggle (Nominal) same                                   contrast=1.00
  light-/whatif   BUTTON (4 more bg-accent-strong buttons: scenario-chain "Apply"/"Save" class, income/expense-card "Add" buttons) same  contrast=1.00
  light-/major-expenses BUTTON .date-range-btn (active preset)  outline rgb(79,70,229) on bg rgb(79,70,229)  contrast=1.00
  light-/major-expenses BUTTON (1 more bg-accent-strong button)                                       contrast=1.00

None of these carry a `focus-visible:ring` / `focus:ring` class (confirmed
by reading `web/templates/pages/whatif.html:26-27`,
`components/whatif/scenario-chain-card.html:50-51`,
`components/whatif/projection-chart.html:16-17`, and the
`components/shared/range-picker.html` preset-button macro directly — plain
`bg-accent-strong ... text-white transition-colors` with no focus
utilities at all) — so BK3's fallback rule legitimately fires on them,
painting `outline: 2px solid rgb(var(--accent))`. But `--accent` and
`--accent-strong` are the same RGB triple in light mode (styles.css lines
35/37, the exact root cause attempt-1 found in the nav), and
`bg-accent-strong` IS these buttons' own fill — so the ring is
**pixel/computed-style-identical to its background, invisible**, on every
one of these controls, in light mode, confirmed both via the ancestor-walk
(non-gradient, directly reported `backgroundColor: rgb(79,70,229)`) and via
