=== FAILURES ===

1. **ACCESSIBILITY.md point 7 (UI component boundaries ≥3:1) / point 12
   (dark-mode-parity clause implies light mode must independently clear
   the same bar) + WCAG 2.2 SC 1.4.11 (non-text contrast) —
   web/static/css/styles.css:300-303 (BK3 attempt-1's fallback rule,
   unmodified by attempt 2) as applied to every `bg-accent-strong`-filled
   button OUTSIDE `<nav>` that carries no focus utility class, light theme
   only.** Confirmed regression vs master on two independently-checked
   controls (`#whatif-new-scenario-toggle` /whatif, active `.date-range-btn`
   preset /major-expenses) plus five more instances found by a full-page
   focusable-element sweep (`#add-chain-step-btn`, the projection chart's
   Nominal toggle, and three more `bg-accent-strong` action buttons on
   /whatif and /major-expenses) — outline color computed as
   pixel-identical to the button's own background (`rgb(79,70,229)` on
   `rgb(79,70,229)`, ratio 1.00:1), where master's browser-default ring
   (`outline: auto`, near-black `rgb(16,16,16)`) cleared 3:1 (3.03:1) at
   every one of these exact locations. Root cause is the same one
   attempt-1 identified (`--accent` and `--accent-strong` are the same RGB
   triple in light mode, styles.css lines 35/37) — attempt 2's fix patches
   only the `<nav>`-scoped instances of this defect and leaves every other
   accent-strong-filled control still broken. This is not a new defect
   class; it is the SAME class the task was dispatched to close, only
   partially closed.

