- The fix for FAILURE 1 likely generalizes cleanly: either (a) extend
  attempt 2's white-ring technique to any element whose own background
  resolves to `--accent-strong` (not just `<nav>` descendants), e.g. a
  `:where([class*="bg-accent-strong"])... { outline-color: white }`
  companion rule, or (b) give the fallback ring a color that never equals
  either `--accent` or `--accent-strong` in light mode (a light-side
  reintroduction of the double-ring browser default, or a distinct
  darker/lighter accent step). Not prescribing the fix — the lead's call.
